      "nets": ["R49.2/R75.1/REG2.24"],
      "observed": "The feedback divider for the MIC26903 5V buck uses R49 = 68k and R75 = 19k6. With the stated 0.8V feedback reference, this gives Vout = 0.8 * (1 + 68/19.6) ≈ 3.58V, not 5V.",
      "expected": "For a 5V output with a 0.8V reference, the divider must have R49/R75 ≈ 5.25. With R49 = 68k, R75 should be about 13k (e.g. 13k), not 19k6.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "R75 19k6 ... R49 68k ... Vout=0.8*(1+R5/R6) (Power sheet)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "5 V rail: A MIC26903YJL-TR synchronous buck regulator steps the battery input down to 5 V. Design notes on this section: ... 'Vout=0.8*(1+R5/R6)'"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The 5V rail will regulate to approximately 3.6V instead of 5V, causing servos, GPS, and USB-UART bridges to malfunction or not operate.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["USB6", "NAVC2"],
      "pins": ["USB6.3", "USB6.2", "NAVC2.44", "NAVC2.45"],
      "nets": ["NET0142", "NET0111"],
      "observed": "USB6 D+ (pin 3) connects through R26 to NET0142, which is NAVC PA11 (USB_DM). USB6 D- (pin 2) connects through R59 to NET0111, which is NAVC PA12 (USB_DP).",
      "expected": "USB D+ should connect to USB_DP (NAVC PA12) and USB D- should connect to USB_DM (NAVC PA11).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "USB6 ... D+ 3 ... R26 22 ... NET0142; D- 2 ... R59 22 ... NET0111 (Connections sheet)"
        },
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "PA11 ... NET0142; PA12 ... NET0111 (NAVC sheet, pins 44 and 45)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The NAVC USB programming/DFU port will not enumerate or will fail because the USB data lines are swapped.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic contains two high-confidence anomalies: the 5V buck feedback divider is set for ~3.6V instead of 5V (R75 = 19k6 with R49 = 68k), and the NAVC USB programming connector has D+/D- swapped."
}

